{%- comment -%}
  Icon for #ka-rail (layout/theme.liquid), repeated vertically down the
  rail. assets/ka-rail-icon.svg is a wide horizontal wordmark (viewBox
  4264x191, ~22:1) - rendered via <img> rather than inlined, since
  inlining it (it embeds two base64 PNGs) 15x over would bloat the page;
  as an <img> the browser fetches/decodes it once and reuses it.

  The wrapper reserves the POST-rotation footprint (narrow/tall) in the
  flex column; the <img> inside keeps its PRE-rotation natural
  proportions (wide/short) and is rotated 90deg around its own center,
  landing exactly inside the wrapper's box. Rotating the img directly
  without this wrapper would rotate its visual appearance but not its
  layout box, so neighboring icons in the column would be spaced as if
  it were still wide/short instead of narrow/tall.
{%- endcomment -%}
<span class="ka-rail__icon-wrap">
  <img
    class="ka-rail__icon"
    src="{{ 'ka-rail-icon.svg' | asset_url }}"
    alt=""
    loading="lazy"
    width="4264"
    height="191"
  >
</span>
